# The Planetary Council's window (CouncWin, see src/ui/councwin.c): how a seat shows a faction's vote and its votes. The Supreme Leader
# proposal (council_p1 after votes_two) shows each faction's number of votes under its portrait. The window's own votes are poked in
# (-1 yea, -2 nay, -3 abstain, -4 and -5 the two other words, a faction's number a vote for it; faction n's is at 0x6ff6d4 + 4n) and the
# seats drawn again (all of them, then the whole window): the five words and a candidate's name in the candidate's colour. The mouse over a
# seat (the hover field at 0x6ff6b4 is poked, and the seat drawn): the picture under the portrait changes; the mouse leaving puts it
# back. A faction with a major atrocity (a poke on its table) shows no votes. The state regions are as in councwin_vote.scene.
# Leave time after each step; the snaps take 2 s each.
